  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Friday 15 January 1926. Both wards were contested: nine candidates for seven seats in the North Ward and seven for five in the South Ward. The Belfast News-Letter prints the result (18 January 1926, p. 7), confirmed by the Irish News the same day. The Irish News (18 January 1926, p. 7) prints the same figures. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026)."
